WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.401 --> 00:00:02.568
-Hey, everybody. Tariq and I are
here in Astoria, Queens,

00:00:02.568 --> 00:00:04.604
at the Welling Court
Mural Project.

00:00:04.604 --> 00:00:06.872
This is one of the most amazing
collections of street art

00:00:06.872 --> 00:00:08.107
in the world made by

00:00:08.107 --> 00:00:10.276
some of the most legendary
street artists ever.

00:00:10.276 --> 00:00:11.677
Let's go talk to one of them.

00:00:11.677 --> 00:00:18.217 line:0%
♪♪

00:00:18.217 --> 00:00:24.790 line:0%
♪♪

00:00:24.790 --> 00:00:26.325
Lady Pink.

00:00:26.325 --> 00:00:28.094
-Hey. How you are?
-Jimmy Fallon. Nice to meet you.

00:00:28.094 --> 00:00:30.497
-Hey. How you doing?
Tariq. Such an honor.

00:00:30.497 --> 00:00:31.664
-What's up?

00:00:31.664 --> 00:00:33.266
-It is such an honor
to meet you and talk.

00:00:33.266 --> 00:00:35.234
Do you prefer Lady Pink or Pink?

00:00:35.234 --> 00:00:37.136
-You can just call me Pink.
That's alright.

00:00:37.136 --> 00:00:41.140
-Well, just off top, I'm so
honored and it's such a pleasure

00:00:41.140 --> 00:00:43.109
to finally get to
meet you in person

00:00:43.109 --> 00:00:46.212
because the "Wild Style,"
a film that you were in --

00:00:46.212 --> 00:00:47.780
How old were you
when you were in that movie?

00:00:47.780 --> 00:00:50.617
-I was 16, 17 years old.
-A teenager.

00:00:50.617 --> 00:00:53.452
A film that came out in 1982

00:00:53.452 --> 00:00:56.856
really is was what inspired me
to become a musician.

00:00:56.856 --> 00:01:00.293
-Well, thank you for being
inspired by our early work.

00:01:00.293 --> 00:01:02.461
-Yeah.
-You know, all the entire world

00:01:02.461 --> 00:01:04.630
has now been inspired by
graffiti and street art.

00:01:04.630 --> 00:01:06.966
-Absolutely.
-What was it like back then?

00:01:06.966 --> 00:01:09.736
How do you start
as a graffiti artist?

00:01:09.736 --> 00:01:13.306
-Well, you start by being
a vandal, by going underground.

00:01:13.306 --> 00:01:15.241
And you learn everything
out in the street.

00:01:15.241 --> 00:01:17.477
And we teach master
to apprentice.

00:01:17.477 --> 00:01:20.179
You don't just wander off
into danger by yourself.

00:01:20.179 --> 00:01:22.448
So you are taught and schooled.

00:01:22.448 --> 00:01:26.019
Graffiti started in New York
way back, maybe '69,

00:01:26.019 --> 00:01:28.053
and all through
the 1970s and '80s,

00:01:28.053 --> 00:01:29.589
the subway trains were painted.

00:01:29.589 --> 00:01:33.960
I started in '79 when it was
already a full-blown movement

00:01:33.960 --> 00:01:37.430
and there was heroes
and myths and legends

00:01:37.430 --> 00:01:38.965
and I had to keep up
with these guys.

00:01:38.965 --> 00:01:41.300
So as a young one, when
everything went above ground,

00:01:41.300 --> 00:01:43.570
there I was at 16.
-Really?

00:01:43.570 --> 00:01:45.705
Tell us about
the Welling Court Mural Project.

00:01:45.705 --> 00:01:47.106
This is amazing.

00:01:47.106 --> 00:01:49.909
-So, this is
in Astoria, Queens, New York,

00:01:49.909 --> 00:01:54.047
and it is a wonderful festival
that has over a hundred artists,

00:01:54.047 --> 00:01:56.248
over a hundred wall spaces.

00:01:56.248 --> 00:01:58.084
You can walk for
blocks and blocks,

00:01:58.084 --> 00:02:01.420
and there's beautiful murals by
artists from all over the world.

00:02:01.420 --> 00:02:02.822
And this is my mural here.

00:02:02.822 --> 00:02:05.090
It's a Black Lives Matter mural.

00:02:05.090 --> 00:02:07.760
-I love that you're now
part of the community.

00:02:07.760 --> 00:02:09.562
You're above ground,
and you're teaching

00:02:09.562 --> 00:02:12.798
young kids as well as adults.

00:02:12.798 --> 00:02:15.168
But everyone, just like,
"Hey, express yourself."

00:02:15.168 --> 00:02:16.469
-Yeah. Absolutely.

00:02:16.469 --> 00:02:18.137
Even you guys can give it a try.

00:02:18.137 --> 00:02:19.772
-Oh, yeah, I'm pretty sure
I can do it.

00:02:19.772 --> 00:02:21.240
[ Laughs ]
-Uh-huh, uh-huh, okay, alright.

00:02:21.240 --> 00:02:23.109
-What do you think?
What do you think?

00:02:23.109 --> 00:02:25.445
I'm a little overdressed,
but I can figure this out.

00:02:25.445 --> 00:02:27.880
-I don't know. I mean, graffiti
is boot camp for artists.

00:02:27.880 --> 00:02:30.249
This isn't like, "Here, honey,
let me show you how it's done."

00:02:30.249 --> 00:02:32.885
This is like you get up there,
you do your thing,

00:02:32.885 --> 00:02:35.254
and don't shame us all.

00:02:35.254 --> 00:02:36.756
-His name is Shameless.

00:02:36.756 --> 00:02:38.491
[ Laughter ]

00:02:38.491 --> 00:02:39.626
-Alright. Alright.

00:02:39.626 --> 00:02:41.160
-So, we're going to go
with Jimmy --

00:02:41.160 --> 00:02:42.662
We're gonna go with
Jimmy and Tariq.

00:02:42.662 --> 00:02:46.065
-Jimmy and Tariq.
Let's get started.

00:02:46.065 --> 00:02:49.001
Background first
and then colors.

00:02:49.001 --> 00:02:50.636
-This is my first time ever
graffitiing.

00:02:50.636 --> 00:02:53.406
-This is so easy to do.
Anyone can do it, man.

00:02:53.406 --> 00:02:54.941
-I feel like I'm going to
get in trouble.

00:02:54.941 --> 00:02:56.342
-You want us
to call the cops on you?

00:02:56.342 --> 00:02:57.943
[ Laughter ]

00:02:57.943 --> 00:03:00.112
Tariq, it looks like you've done
this before.

00:03:00.112 --> 00:03:01.847
-I may have.
-[ Laughs ]

00:03:01.847 --> 00:03:03.383
-How are you doing it so fast?

00:03:03.383 --> 00:03:04.984
-Thinking about them po-po.

00:03:04.984 --> 00:03:07.853 line:0%
♪♪

00:03:07.853 --> 00:03:09.555
[ Horn honks ]

00:03:09.555 --> 00:03:11.557
-I'm working on it.
You'll love it at the end!

00:03:11.557 --> 00:03:13.259
Don't honk!
-That yellow is good.

00:03:13.259 --> 00:03:14.694
-Yellow is great.

00:03:14.694 --> 00:03:15.828
Copying my yellow?

00:03:15.828 --> 00:03:17.864
-I think so, man.

00:03:17.864 --> 00:03:20.599
-Wow, nice.

00:03:20.599 --> 00:03:23.235
Tariq did a dot first,
so I don't know.

00:03:23.235 --> 00:03:24.903
-He's, like, taking
all my moves.

00:03:24.903 --> 00:03:26.606
-So, when artists paint
together, they got to

00:03:26.606 --> 00:03:29.374
communicate because their pieces
kind of go together.

00:03:29.374 --> 00:03:30.810
-We're communicating.

00:03:30.810 --> 00:03:34.080
It's unspoken, our relationship.

00:03:34.080 --> 00:03:37.249
-Take that yellow
that you have going on.

00:03:37.249 --> 00:03:39.351
So go lines straight up.

00:03:39.351 --> 00:03:40.886
Lines, lines, lines.

00:03:40.886 --> 00:03:43.189
-Oh, yeah. Like a little bleed.

00:03:43.189 --> 00:03:45.291
-You got it, Tariq.

00:03:45.291 --> 00:03:47.125
Ooh, you look like a pro now.

00:03:47.125 --> 00:03:48.894
Look at you outlining.

00:03:48.894 --> 00:03:50.429
-That's not bad, right?
That was good.

00:03:50.429 --> 00:03:52.231
Are we rolling on that?

00:03:52.231 --> 00:03:54.867
-When we painted on the subway
train, there was no ladders.

00:03:54.867 --> 00:03:57.536
You had to hang out the window,
paint upside down.

00:03:57.536 --> 00:04:00.439
-I used to see graffiti that
would make the things move,

00:04:00.439 --> 00:04:02.675
like shapes move up and down
when the train would move.

00:04:02.675 --> 00:04:03.876
-It was magic.

00:04:03.876 --> 00:04:05.577
What did you write down there?
Black Thought?

00:04:05.577 --> 00:04:08.948
-Black Thought, yeah.

00:04:08.948 --> 00:04:10.483
-Jimmy.

00:04:10.483 --> 00:04:12.485
-I think I'm done.
-You're fast.

00:04:12.485 --> 00:04:14.520
-In and out.
-You guys did an awesome job.

00:04:14.520 --> 00:04:15.821
I'm so proud.

00:04:15.821 --> 00:04:17.156
-I love it.
-You might have a future.

00:04:17.156 --> 00:04:18.391
[ Laughter ]

00:04:18.391 --> 00:04:19.892
-Lady, would you do me
the honor?

00:04:19.892 --> 00:04:21.627
Can you just --
-Sure.

00:04:21.627 --> 00:04:26.031 line:0%
♪♪

00:04:26.031 --> 00:04:27.833
-I love this. Come on.

00:04:27.833 --> 00:04:29.668
Tariq, you want to get in?

00:04:29.668 --> 00:04:30.803
That's it right there.

00:04:30.803 --> 00:04:32.271
I love it.
-I see!

00:04:32.271 --> 00:04:34.473
-That's it!
Queens, that's a wrap.

00:04:34.473 --> 00:04:41.080 line:0%
♪♪

